<!--
	Rhubarb, the currency (feature-spec §6a) - general item 1: the icon is the plant the currency is named
	after, not a generic coin. A coin said nothing about "Rhubarb", which is why the amount had to spell out
	an abbreviation next to it; a rhubarb does, so the abbreviation is gone from the label.

	Two stalks under a broad, deeply lobed leaf. The lobes are exaggerated well past life size because the
	whole thing is a single flat fill at 18-20dp: the silhouette is the only cue there is, and a smooth leaf
	at that size is just an oval.

	The fill stays white and is tinted at the call site, so it follows light/dark and any board theme.
-->
